* SSM2164/TL072 integrator with a J111 capacitor-reset switch.
* The VCA input current is fixed; the J111 provides the fast flyback.
.include ..\..\models\2164\SSM2164.lib
.include ..\..\models\tl072\TL072.lib
.include ..\..\models\lm393\LM393.lib
.include ..\..\models\j11\J111.lib

VCC VCC 0 15
VEE VEE 0 -15
VCV CV 0 0.774
.param MIX=0.5 RPOT=100k

* Constant input voltage/current into SSM2164 channel 1.
VIN IN 0 1
RIN IN NDRIVE 30k
RSHUNT NDRIVE NCOMP 500
CCOMP NCOMP 0 560p
VIMON NDRIVE IIN1 0

* Comparator A switches at the negative ramp limit and reset level.
* Comparator B inverts HYST to drive the J111 gate switch.
RPU1 HYST VCC 10k
RPU2 RESET VCC 10k
RTH VEE VTH 1Meg
RREF VTH 0 100k
RFB VTH RESET 1Meg
* LM393 pin order: OUT1, IN1-, IN1+, VEE, IN2+, IN2-, OUT2, VCC.
XU3 HYST VTH CAP VEE 0 HYST RESET VCC LM393

* Unused SSM2164 channels are grounded directly at the package pins.
VOMON IOUT1 SUM 0
* SSM2164 pin order: MODE, IIN1, VC1, IOUT1, IOUT2, VC2, IIN2, GND,
* VEE, IIN3, VC3, IOUT3, IOUT4, VC4, IIN4, VCC.
XU1 0 IIN1 CV IOUT1 0 0 0 0 VEE 0 0 0 0 0 0 VCC SSM2164

CFB CAP SUM 560p IC=0
* Scale the comparator square wave into the TL072 input common-mode range.
RSQ1 RESET SQDIV 20k
RSQ2 SQDIV 0 10k
* RV1 crossfades CAP (MIX=0) to the scaled comparator square (MIX=1).
RPOT1 CAP MIXW {max(1,RPOT*MIX)}
RPOT2 MIXW SQDIV {max(1,RPOT*(1-MIX))}
* TL072 channel 2 is a unity-gain buffer for the high-impedance pot wiper.
XU2 CAP SUM 0 VEE MIXW MIXOUT MIXOUT VCC TL072

* The depletion JFET is pinched off at -15 V gate bias. RESET rises during
* flyback and forward-biases its gate near 0 V.
RGATE RESET GATE 100k
RRESET CAP DRESET 220
VQMON DRESET QDRAIN 0
* J111 pin order: Drain, Gate, Source.
XQ1 QDRAIN GATE SUM J111

.save V(CAP) V(SUM) V(IN) V(CV) V(HYST) V(RESET) V(VTH) V(GATE) V(DRESET) V(SQDIV) V(MIXW) V(MIXOUT) V(IOUT1) I(VIMON) I(VOMON) I(VQMON)
.tran 0 10m 0 50n uic
.options TNOM=25 TEMP=25 method=gear
.end
